irgsh for Debian
================

IRGSH is an all-in-one tool for creating and maintaining Debian-derived
GNU/Linux distributions.

Initial Setup
-------------

After installation, you need to perform the following steps:

1. Install and configure Redis server:

   sudo apt-get install redis-server
   sudo systemctl start redis-server
   sudo systemctl enable redis-server

2. Configure IRGSH by editing /etc/irgsh/config.yaml according to your needs.

3. Provision the dedicated builder account's subordinate UID and GID ranges.
   The package creates irgsh-builder, but does not allocate these ranges.
   Inspect /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid, choose non-overlapping ranges of at
   least 65536 IDs, then replace START-END below:

   sudo usermod --add-subuids START-END --add-subgids START-END irgsh-builder

4. Initialize the native builder base under its dedicated account:

   sudo -u irgsh-builder irgsh-builder -c /etc/irgsh/config.yaml init-base

   Update it later with the same account and config using update-base.
   sbuild, mmdebstrap, and the uidmap helpers require unprivileged user
   namespaces. Do not run builder commands as root or add this account to
   privileged groups. The builder does not need signing keys or GNUPGHOME.

5. For the repository component, initialize it:

   sudo -u irgsh irgsh-repo -c /etc/irgsh/config.yaml init

The interactive /usr/share/irgsh/init.sh also offers destructive shared-state,
GPG, and repository initialization. Use it only during an approved initial
setup on an isolated host. Its builder base operation uses irgsh-builder.

For host requirements, existing-service migration, additional instances,
rollback, and target-host evidence, follow docs/rootless-builder.md in the
matching source revision:
https://github.com/BlankOn/irgsh-go/blob/main/docs/rootless-builder.md

Starting Services
-----------------

You can start the IRGSH services with:

   sudo systemctl start irgsh-chief
   sudo systemctl start irgsh-builder
   sudo systemctl start irgsh-repo
   sudo systemctl start irgsh-iso   # optional

To enable them at boot:

   sudo systemctl enable irgsh-chief
   sudo systemctl enable irgsh-builder
   sudo systemctl enable irgsh-repo

Logs
----

Service logs are available at:
   /var/log/irgsh/chief.log
   /var/log/irgsh/builder.log
   /var/log/irgsh/repo.log
   /var/log/irgsh/iso.log

Using the CLI
-------------

Configure the CLI tool to point to your IRGSH chief instance:

   irgsh-cli config --chief http://localhost:8080 --key YOUR_GPG_KEY_ID

Submit a package build job:

   irgsh-cli package submit --source SOURCE_URL --package PACKAGE_URL

For more information, visit:
https://github.com/BlankOn/irgsh-go

